# E4-R12 (N02): stable byte contract for hash-constrained evolution evidence.
#
# The evolution ledger records sha256 OVER RAW FILE BYTES (LF). A fresh
# Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true would rewrite these text files to
# CRLF and break every recorded digest (verified: an all-CRLF read of the
# ledger refs produces 11 DIGEST_MISMATCH). These rules force LF checkout on
# every platform — the storage contract is "git blob bytes", never a silent
# normalization inside the verifier (historical raw-byte digests stay valid).
docs/evolution/*.json text eol=lf
benchmarks/results/**/*.json text eol=lf

# E4-R84: the campaign evidence fixture is byte-pinned. Its committed root
# digest (asserted in packages/evaluation/src/campaign-validate.test.ts) and its
# generator's `--check` mode both compare bytes, so a Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true must not rewrite it to CRLF.
scripts/benchmark/fixtures/r84-campaign/** text eol=lf

# E4-R84: the CI workflow blob was historically stored WITH CRLF (`git ls-files
# --eol` reported `i/crlf`), so every added line carried a CR and
# `git diff --check` reported it as trailing whitespace — commit 0ca421e
# produced 194 such warnings on this one file. The file is plain-text YAML and
# nothing depends on its stored bytes, so pin it to LF; this is the same fix the
# two rules above already apply to their own files.
.github/workflows/*.yml text eol=lf